    {
      "id": "a1_u06_l01",
      "level": "A1",
      "unit": 6,
      "title": "Au petit-déjeuner",
      "description": "Name French breakfast foods and say what you eat and drink.",
      "estimatedMinutes": 13,
      "sections": [
        {
          "type": "learn",
          "title": "Learn",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "heading": "A French breakfast",
              "body": "The French breakfast — le petit-déjeuner — is usually simple and sweet: bread or a croissant, butter, jam, and a hot drink. To say what you eat and drink, use \"je mange\" (I eat) and \"je bois\" (I drink).",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Je mange du pain avec du beurre.", "english": "I eat bread with butter." },
                { "french": "Je bois du thé.", "english": "I drink tea." },
                { "french": "Il mange un croissant.", "english": "He eats a croissant." },
                { "french": "Elle boit du jus d'orange.", "english": "She drinks some orange juice." },
                { "french": "Je mange une tartine avec du miel.", "english": "I eat a slice of bread with honey." }
              ],
              "tip": "Many French people dip their croissant or tartine straight into their coffee — it's completely normal!"
            }
          ]
        },
